{
  "title": "The if Statement — A Fork in the Road",
  "subtitle": "Making Decisions with Comparison Operators",
  "topic": "4.1 • THE IF STATEMENT",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      4.1 • Decision Making\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>if</hlt> Statement & Comparisons\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      In real life, we make decisions constantly: <em>\"If it rains, take an umbrella\"</em> or <em>\"If speed is over 60, slow down\"</em>. The <hlt>if</hlt> statement gives your Python programs this exact power!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"lesson-ref-card\">\n    <div class=\"lesson-ref-header\">\n      <span class=\"ref-badge\">PREVIOUS KNOWLEDGE</span>\n      <span class=\"lesson-ref-title\">Connecting to Earlier Concepts</span>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"lesson-ref-desc\">\n      In earlier chapters, we stored numbers in variables and evaluated mathematical calculations. Now we compare those values to make dynamic choices!\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=3&sub=1&ref_from=1_5_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Variables & Values (Lesson 3.1) →</a>\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=4&sub=1&ref_from=1_5_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Basic Math & Precedence (Lesson 4.1) →</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      1. Real-World Analogy\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The Security Checkpoint Gate\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      Think of an <hlt>if</hlt> statement as a security guard at an airport gate. The guard asks a True/False question (e.g., <em>\"Is your boarding pass valid?\"</em>). If the answer is <strong>True</strong>, you pass through the gate. If the answer is <strong>False</strong>, the guard ignores the gate passage and moves to the next instruction.\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 12px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      • <strong>Condition evaluates to True:</strong> Python enters the indented block and runs the code.<br/>\n      • <strong>Condition evaluates to False:</strong> Python completely skips the indented block and continues downward.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #93c5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      2. The 6 Comparison Operators\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      How Python Compares Values\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">\n      Comparisons always produce a Boolean result: either <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800;\">\n        <code>==</code> Equal to<br/><span style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: #555;\">5 == 5 is True</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800;\">\n        <code>!=</code> Not equal to<br/><span style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: #555;\">5 != 3 is True</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800;\">\n        <code>&gt;</code> Greater than<br/><span style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: #555;\">10 &gt; 4 is True</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800;\">\n        <code>&lt;</code> Less than<br/><span style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: #555;\">2 &lt; 9 is True</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800;\">\n        <code>&gt;=</code> Greater or equal<br/><span style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: #555;\">18 &gt;= 18 is True</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800;\">\n        <code>&lt;=</code> Less or equal<br/><span style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: #555;\">15 &lt;= 20 is True</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      speed = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">75</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">if</span> speed &gt; <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">60</span>:<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Over speed limit! Slow down.\"</span>)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Runs because 75 &gt; 60 is True</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #86efac; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      3. Practical Example: Thermostat Alarm\n    </span>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      Consider a smart home thermostat checking the room temperature. When temperature exceeds 30 degrees Celsius, it triggers cooling:\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      temp = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">34.5</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">if</span> temp &gt;= <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">30.0</span>:<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"AC Activated: Cooling Room\"</span>)<br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"System Check Complete\"</span>)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Unindented: Always runs</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}